From 8c31732ac8f20785bebf2573c1cb0c66b6d76e01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:21:44 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Spatiand: passwords and passkeys in SpatiKey

Chromium's password store is wrapped so nothing of a login is kept here: a login form is told there
may be one, choosing it asks the vault with a touch, and a password to save goes to the vault. Passkeys
are device/fido/spatikey, the platform authenticator on Linux. Manage passwords opens SpatiKey's window.
No signing in to the browser with a Google account: a Google login stays on the page.
